return Optional.ofNullable(jsonNode.get(SCHEMA_TAG)).map(schemaTag -> {
    String schemaTagValue = schemaTag.asText();
    String schemaUri = JsonSchemaFactory.normalizeMetaSchemaUri(schemaTagValue);
    return SpecVersion.VersionFlag.fromId(schemaUri).orElseThrow(() -> new JsonSchemaException("'" + schemaTagValue + "' is unrecognizable schema"));
});

So branches: if jsonNode.get("$schema") returns null -> Optional.empty(). That's one branch.

If not null, then map runs. Inside map: schemaTagValue extracted. Then normalizeMetaSchemaUri may transform. Need to test when fromId returns a VersionFlag (valid schema) vs when it throws (unrecognizable). So need cases:

1. No $schema field -> expect Optional.empty.

2. $schema present with recognizable schema URI -> expect Optional.of(VersionFlag) (e.g., draft-07). Need to know what IDs are recognized. In SpecVersion.VersionFlag, typical IDs: "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#" etc. We'll assume fromId can parse normalized URI. Use a known one.

3. $schema present with unrecognizable schema -> expect JsonSchemaException thrown from map, causing Optional.map will throw, so method will propagate exception. So test expects exception.

Also test that normalizeMetaSchemaUri is called; we can simulate by providing a schema tag that needs normalization, e.g., "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#" maybe unchanged. Or a variant "draft-07" maybe normalized to full URI. Not needed for branch coverage but can test.

